  "nl_text": "The rschema_0400 database is designed to manage user interactions and book borrowing within a community. The database consists of six tables: Role, Book, User, Notification, User_Establishes_Friend_Relationship, and User_Borrows_Book. The Role table stores information about different roles, including a unique role ID, a descriptive name, and a brief description. The Book table contains details about each book, such as its title, author, category, publication date, and publisher. The User table represents individual users, with attributes like their college affiliation, email, password, registration time, and a unique user ID, which is linked to a specific role through the Role_ID foreign key. The Notification table stores notifications sent by users, including the content, title, release date, and the user ID of the publisher. The User_Establishes_Friend_Relationship table tracks friendships between users, with each relationship having a creation time and referencing the IDs of both users involved. The User_Borrows_Book table records when a user borrows a book, including the book ID, borrow and return times, and the user ID, with both the book and user IDs serving as composite primary keys to ensure uniqueness.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description:\nThis is an online instant messaging service platform system. In terms of role management, the system supports the management of different user roles such as students, teachers, and colleges, each with its corresponding role name and permission settings. In user management, the system records each user’s basic information, including a unique User ID, Username, Password, College, Email, and Registration Time, while also assigning the appropriate role to each user. In book management, the system maintains book information, including Book ID, Book Name, Author, Publisher, Publication Date, and Book Category, and supports users borrowing multiple books. In notification management, the system supports users in publishing and managing notification information. Each notification includes Notification ID, Notification Title, Notification Content, Publisher ID, and Release Date. All users can serve as the publisher of notifications.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0400.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0400\nCREATE TABLE `Role` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `college_affiliation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `Role` (`role_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Notification` (\n  `notification_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`notification_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Establishes_Friend_Relationship` (\n  `user_id_1` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id_2` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id_1`, `user_id_2`),\n  CONSTRAINT `friendship_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id_1`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `friendship_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id_2`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Borrows_Book` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrow_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `return_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `borrows_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `borrows_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `Book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
